<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-10-13.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="010637"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010637" label="[01:06:37]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: can you please merge <a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/bootstrap-seeds/pull/45">https://github.com/oriansj/bootstrap-seeds/pull/45</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="010710"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#010710" label="[01:07:10]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I've reviewed new bootstrap seed, looks fine appart from some comments which I have now fixed</span></div><div class="line" id="011017"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011017" label="[01:10:17]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">some of that stuff in this hex0 seed can be ported to other arches...</span></div><div class="line" id="011018"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011018" label="[01:10:18]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I was aware of a couple of possible tricks before but this new seed goes far beyond that...</span></div><div class="line" id="011032"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011032" label="[01:10:32]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, 190 bytes on x86 means only 106 bytes of actual code</span></div><div class="line" id="011054"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011054" label="[01:10:54]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">though some of the tricks are x86 specific there</span></div><div class="line" id="011153"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#011153" label="[01:11:53]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">in a couple of places some registers just have required values for x86 syscall numbers</span></div><div class="line" id="013222"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#013222" label="[01:32:22]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: reviewed and merged.</span></div><div class="line" id="013234"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013234" label="[01:32:34]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">thanks</span></div><div class="line" id="013829"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#013829" label="[01:38:29]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well; there are a great many potential optimizations that could be done for the bootstrap-seeds (kaem-optional-seed could be shrunk down to under 256bytes if one got creative) I've opted for easy to reason about by default and left the clever optimizations to people better at code golf than I.</span></div><div class="line" id="013927"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013927" label="[01:39:27]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, probably hard to reduce hex0_x86 seed further</span></div><div class="line" id="013932"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#013932" label="[01:39:32]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but yes, kaem is not super optimized</span></div><div class="line" id="055514"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#055514" label="[05:55:14]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://pileofhacks.dev/post/the-optimised-version-of-7-zip-cant-be-built-from-source/">https://pileofhacks.dev/post/the-optimised-version-of-7-zip-cant-be-built-from-source/</a>  <a rel="nofollow" href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=41824784">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=41824784</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="055704"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#055704" label="[05:57:04]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message">asmc isn't immediately bootstrappable</span></div><div class="line" id="094628"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#094628" label="[09:46:28]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; It's assembler though ...</span></div><div class="line" id="094631"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#094631" label="[09:46:31]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; How hard can it be to compile with another one</span></div><div class="line" id="094650"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#094650" label="[09:46:50]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Probably need to adjust makefiles and perhaps some asm syntax</span></div><div class="line" id="094704"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#094704" label="[09:47:04]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message">from #debian-devel &lt;helmut&gt; I happen to have looked into nim packaging. My understanding is that nim can be compiled to C and the nim source package includes the compilied C sources, builds nim from that and then uses nim to build nim. Is that actually a good way to bootstrap it?</span></div><div class="line" id="094751"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#094751" label="[09:47:51]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Though yes, it is an annoying case of poor documented build</span></div><div class="line" id="095010"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#095010" label="[09:50:10]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ACTION mentioned <a rel="nofollow" href="https://bootstrapping.miraheze.org/wiki/Bootstrapping_Nim">https://bootstrapping.miraheze.org/wiki/Bootstrapping_Nim</a>  to helmut</span></div><div class="line" id="095010"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#095010" label="[09:50:10]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I'm not on that channel (#debian-devel) but I guess folks here would not consider that a good way of bootstrappng</span></div><div class="line" id="095018"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#095018" label="[09:50:18]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">thanks</span></div><div class="line" id="095053"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#095053" label="[09:50:53]">&lt;nimaje&gt;</a></span><span class="message">that blog post says that asmc is a nasm compatible assembler, but only tries to replace it with jwasm, from which asmc was apparently forked from, not idea why nasm wasn't tried, shouldn't that be the first idea there?</span></div><div class="line" id="095318"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#095318" label="[09:53:18]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah, my thought was to use nasm too before I've read that blog</span></div><div class="line" id="095324"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#095324" label="[09:53:24]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">so no idea either why it wasn't tried</span></div><div class="line" id="095610"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#095610" label="[09:56:10]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">dozer seems to be progressing nicerly with more than one contributor now: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://codeberg.org/notgull/dozer/commits/branch/main">https://codeberg.org/notgull/dozer/commits/branch/main</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="130705"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#130705" label="[13:07:05]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">pabs3: yeah Nim still requires a great deal more work before it can be properly bootstrapped. As generated C sources are clearly not human written nor the preferred form for modification.</span></div><div class="line" id="130754"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#130754" label="[13:07:54]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: thanks for the link</span></div><br /></div></body></html>